.TH MEMWATCHER 8 "September 2026" "memwatcher 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
memwatcher \- experimental continuous online physical-memory tester
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memwatcher info
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B memwatcher selftest
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B memwatcher scan --yes-i-understand
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Memwatcher slowly asks its companion kernel module to isolate one physical
pageblock at a time. A disposable, low-priority process writes and verifies
memory-test patterns. Good pages return to Linux; suspect or uncertain pages
remain allocated until reboot.
.PP
This is destructive, experimental kernel software. Test it only in a disposable
virtual machine before considering lab hardware. It is not a substitute for ECC,
EDAC monitoring, backups, or an offline memory test.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Show ABI, pageblock size, counters, and queryable quarantined PFNs.
.TP
.B selftest
Run the pattern engine on ordinary allocated process memory. This does not claim
physical pages through the module.
.TP
.B scan
Enumerate online physical memory and attempt a destructive pageblock sweep.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --device " path"
Device node. Default is /dev/memwatcher.
.TP
.BI --state " path"
Append-only scan ledger. Default is /var/lib/memwatcher/state.tsv.
.TP
.BI --interval " seconds"
Nonnegative delay between pageblock attempts. Default is 10.
.TP
.BI --passes " count"
Number of sweeps. Default is 1.
.TP
.B --forever
Repeat sweeps until SIGINT or SIGTERM.
.TP
.BI --start-pfn " pfn"
First PFN in a restricted range; requires --end-pfn.
.TP
.BI --end-pfn " pfn"
Exclusive end PFN in a restricted range; requires --start-pfn.
.TP
.B --quick
Use a reduced fixed-pattern set. March and address-derived tests still run.
.TP
.B --no-cache-flush
Permit a cache-resident test. This is weaker and not recommended.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Enumerate candidate pageblocks without opening the kernel device.
.TP
.B --yes-i-understand
Mandatory acknowledgement for a destructive scan.
.TP
.BI --mib " count"
Allocation size for selftest. Default is 16 MiB.
.SH SAFETY
The module is disarmed unless loaded with enabled=1. Opening the device requires
CAP_SYS_RAWIO. If a test worker crashes or abandons a claim, the entire claimed
pageblock is retained. Once quarantine occurs, module removal and system suspend
are intentionally prevented until reboot.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/memwatcher
Restricted kernel-module interface.
.TP
.I /var/lib/memwatcher/state.tsv
Default append-only result ledger.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR memtester (8),
.BR systemd.service (5)
